      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/resources/string-resource.html#Plurals\n\nThe entire thing is worth reading but the most illuminating paragraph on your very specific question is :\n\n  The selection of which string to use is made solely based on grammatical necessity. In\n  English, a string for zero is ignored even if the quantity is 0, because 0 isn\u0027t\n  grammatically different from 2, or any other number except 1 (\"zero books\", \"one book\", \"two\n  books\", and so on). Conversely, in Korean only the other string is ever used.",
